{
  "title": "Namaz for Settling Needs",
  "data": "At midnight, bathe yourself (ghusl) and offer a two-unit prayer. In both units, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) five hundred times.\nAfter repeating Surah al-Tawhid in the second unit, recite the last verses of [Surah al-Hashr](A63) (59:21-24, from \"Law anzalnaa haadhal Qur'aana...\") and then the first six verses of [Surah al-Hadid](A61).\nWhile still standing, repeat the following verse one thousand times:\nاِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَاِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِيْنُ\nIYYAAKA NA'BUDU WA IYYAAKA NASTA'EEN\nYou alone do we worship, and You alone do we ask for help.\nThen complete your prayer and praise Almighty Allah.",
  "merits": "The following is quoted from the book of Makarim al-Akhlaq.\nIf your need is not settled, repeat this prayer; if it is still not settled, repeat it once more, and your need will be settled, Allah willing."
}
